**Status**: Approved
**Author**: NMG
**Related Spec**: specs/512-file-generated-bug-fix-changelog-lines-under-fixed/

# File: scripts/__tests__/sdlc-deliver.test.mjs
# Generated from: specs/519-insert-a-blank-line-between-an-empty-matching-changelog-heading-and-the-generated-bullet/requirements.md
Feature: Generated CHANGELOG bullet spacing under a matching heading

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: An empty trailing Fixed heading gets one blank line before the generated bullet
    Given issue #42 titled "Deliver verified changes" is labelled "bug" with no BREAKING declaration
    And CHANGELOG.md [Unreleased] contains only "### Fixed" followed by blank lines
    When prepare-version runs for issue #42
    Then the new release section ends with "### Fixed", one blank line, and "- Deliver verified changes (#42)"
    And the new release section contains "### Fixed" exactly once

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: An empty Fixed heading followed by another section gets one blank line on each side of the generated bullet
    Given issue #42 titled "Deliver verified changes" is labelled "bug" with no BREAKING declaration
    And CHANGELOG.md [Unreleased] contains "### Fixed" with only blank lines beneath it, then "### Changed" with "- Renamed the option (#8)"
    When prepare-version runs for issue #42
    Then the new release section contains "### Fixed", one blank line, "- Deliver verified changes (#42)", one blank line, then "### Changed"
    And the "### Changed" section still contains "- Renamed the option (#8)"

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: A populated Fixed section receives the generated bullet after its last bullet
    Given issue #42 titled "Deliver verified changes" is labelled "bug" with no BREAKING declaration
    And CHANGELOG.md [Unreleased] contains "### Fixed" with "- Corrected the widget (#7)", then "### Changed" with "- Renamed the option (#8)"
    When prepare-version runs for issue #42
    Then "- Deliver verified changes (#42)" directly follows "- Corrected the widget (#7)" with no blank line between them

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: A section without a matching heading gets a new Fixed heading as before
    Given issue #42 titled "Deliver verified changes" is labelled "bug" with no BREAKING declaration
    And CHANGELOG.md has an empty [Unreleased] section
    When prepare-version runs for issue #42
    Then the new release section ends with "### Fixed", one blank line, and "- Deliver verified changes (#42)"
